# =============================================================================
# Called & Sent — frontend environment variables
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# All VITE_* variables are PUBLIC and baked into the client bundle at build
# time. Never put secrets here. Server-side bindings (D1, R2, BETTER_AUTH_URL,
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY, Neon) are configured separately — see
# docs/dev.md and FUNCTIONS_ENV.md.
# =============================================================================

# Mapbox public token (map tiles + terrain). Get one at
# https://account.mapbox.com/ — create a free account, copy your default
# public token, or scope a new token to the map styles this app uses.
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=your_mapbox_token_here

# Neon Managed Better Auth origin — the base URL of the Better Auth instance
# that owns credentials. WITHOUT THIS the login page renders but every auth
# call fails: the app cannot create the auth client, sessions never resolve,
# and dashboard/profile routes are dead (they redirect to /login forever).
#
# Set it to the origin of your deployed Better Auth instance, e.g.
#     VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL=https://your-project.neon.auth
# or your local auth server origin when running the auth stack locally.
# This must stay in sync with BETTER_AUTH_URL in .dev.vars (see
# FUNCTIONS_ENV.md — same origin, two bindings).
VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL=your_neon_auth_url_here

# Cloudflare Turnstile site key (PUBLIC — safe to commit). Used by the
# SupportModal contact form to block spam. Create a widget at
# https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/turnstile and add every hostname
# you develop on (e.g. http://localhost:5173) to its list of allowed origins.
#
# Leave this BLANK (remove the line) to fall back to the site key bundled in
# src/features/profile/SupportModal.tsx. Setting an invalid value here breaks
# the widget — a real key or nothing at all.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
